# No AI Attribution

Git commits must represent the repository owner only.

Never add any AI attribution to commits.

Forbidden trailers include (but are not limited to):

```
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

Co-authored-by: OpenAI

Generated-by:

AI-assisted:

Created-with-AI:
```

Rules:

- Never append AI attribution trailers.
- Never mention Cursor in commit messages.
- Never mention ChatGPT in commit messages.
- Never include generated-by metadata.
- Never modify Git author identity.
- Never overwrite the user's Git configuration.

If any extension, tool, or hook automatically injects AI attribution:

- Remove it before the commit is finalized.
- If the commit is still local and unpushed, amend it to remove the trailer.
- Never push commits containing AI attribution unless explicitly requested by the repository owner.